Third-party source attribution

The source files in sparse_grt_backend and sparse_grt_tracer are derived from
NVIDIA 3DGRUT and this project's research fork. Original Apache-2.0 copyright
headers have been retained. See licenses/3DGRUT-Apache-2.0.txt.

The MCMC implementation also credits gsplat and 3D Gaussian Splatting as Markov
Chain Monte Carlo in its source header. These acknowledgements are preserved.

The standalone migration changes Python namespaces, removes eager GUI/GUT
imports, builds the reference CUDA backend from packaged sources, and replaces
the experiment-specific bootstrap with a headless initializer. Existing CUDA
and C++ source calculations are preserved. provenance/standalone_vendor.json
records the originating research-fork sources and their hashes.

NVIDIA OptiX headers are an external dependency, fetched from the pinned official
repository with their original LICENSE.txt. They are not part of this package's
source distribution or wheel. CUDA and the NVIDIA GPU driver are external
dependencies as well.

This notice records third-party attribution. It does not assign a public license
